invariant: INV-67
file: mldsa_vector.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mldsa-vector
reason: the signer's dispatch drops its test of the multiply bit, so a
  session whose caller states nothing about the multiply runs the lanes'
  32x32 products on s1, s2, t0, y and c, whose timing that caller has not
  stated. Every byte stays right, so no vector notices.
  bin/mldsa_runtime_test counts the calls into the lanes under each
  ch_cfg.cpu value and requires none from the signer without the bit.
  The script runs the binary for arm64 under qemu-aarch64 and for x86-64
  under qemu-x86_64.

--- old
    uint32_t need = secret ? CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY : 0;
--- new
    uint32_t need = secret > 1 ? CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY : 0;
